><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c: </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Employing functional calibrations for MIMU-based thorax&#xD;and lumbar joint angle calculations did not significantly&#xD;decrease measurement differences when compared with&#xD;concurrently collected 3D retro-reflective derived angles.&#xD;Functional calibration does not appear necessary for MIMU&#xD;thorax and lumbar angle measurements for uni-planar and&#xD;high-speed, sport-specific multi-planar movements.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
